      "crop_sha256": "5592b031bf3aa70e8f58560a7d9c35f7eb643afa0d5bdc0b0509d584ef8d5b91",
      "raw_text": "For starters, z = 0, c = 1. So Z = 1. First loop: Z = 1 2 + 1 = 2. Second loop: Z = 2 2 + 1 = 5. Third loop: Z = 5 2 + 1 = 26. Fourth loop: Z = 26 2 + 1 … and so on.",
      "normalized_text": "",
      "latex": null,
      "mathml": null,
      "fidelity_status": "PENDING_VISUAL_AUDIT",
      "derivation_role": null,
      "context_before": [
        {
          "node_id": "d3086999-ff69-543f-9340-3cc3a5b02f4b",
          "page_index": 42,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "I once set my computer to work out the higher terms (about the limit of my programming ability) and it produced only two more values before it had to start approximating. Starting from the beginning we get:"
        },
        {
          "node_id": "0f36ab0d-df27-5ad6-9ebb-ef79af6b912d",
          "page_index": 42,
          "block_type": "heading",
          "text": "The indescribable M-set"
        }
      ],
      "context_after": [
        {
          "node_id": "60451e60-905c-5cbd-b7d4-14a30f49311a",
          "page_index": 42,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "You should be able to do it in your head - for the first few steps. But after a few dozen even a supercomputer may blow a gasket."
        },
        {
          "node_id": "17522aa2-91f5-5c00-b1c3-713b41c55054",
          "page_index": 42,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "One might have guessed that, from the nature of the equation. But no-one could possibly have intuited its real appearance: if the question had been put to me in my virginal pre-Mandelbrot days, I would probably have hazarded: 'Something like an ellipse, squashed along the Y-axis.' I might even (though I doubt it) have correctly guessed that it would be shifted towards the left, or minus, direction."
        }
      ],
      "canonicality_cues": [
