          "text": "Fig. 3.12 below: The Mandelbrot Set, surrounded by its equipotential curves."
        },
        {
          "node_id": "f74be31d-b456-52f0-a1b2-de80799eb02b",
          "page_index": 63,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "More generally, the coordinates u k and v k of C k are obtained from u k -1 and v k -1 by the so-called 'iterative formulas'"
        }
      ],
      "context_after": [
        {
          "node_id": "d0666589-af59-51c4-9156-17265399ff56",
          "page_index": 63,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "Here is how the Mandelbrot Set is constructed. Take a starting point C 0 in the plane of coordinates u 0 and v 0 . From the coordinate of C 0 , form a second point C 1 of coordinates u 1 = u 0 2 -v 0 2 + u 0"
        },
        {
          "node_id": "5257cbf7-3303-5b63-ad93-c7cb76924ec4",
          "page_index": 63,
          "block_type": "heading",
          "text": "Constructing the Mandelbrot Set"
        }
      ],
