        {
          "node_id": "12b43056-4d15-5827-ab98-2b11597b6490",
          "page_index": 88,
          "block_type": "text",
          "text": "The arrow can be read as 'goes to' or 'becomes', for what this rule represents is a transformation of two-dimensional space; the letters z and c by convention indicate generic points in this space, with z being variable and c constant. In other words, the rule transforms the point z to another point in the space, while leaving c unchanged. This twodimensional space inhabited by z and c, the home of the Mandelbrot Set and Julia Sets, is central to mathematics, from quantum mechanics to number theory."
        }
      ],
      "context_after": [
        {
